✅ Addressed in commits ac19cb0 to 8c757a2

If now or in future you don't want to maintain this hand-rolled version, or want to do more accurate assertions against actual DOM <ins>**updates**</ins>, see https://github.com/AriPerkkio/extend-to-be-announced?tab=readme-ov-file#vitest. It's 0 external dependency solution (well 1 direct dep on `aria-live-capture` which is 0 deps) that provides everything out-of-the-box. 


```ts
// setup.ts
import 'extend-to-be-announced/vitest';

// test
expect('Loading').toBeAnnounced('polite');
expect('Error').toBeAnnounced('assertive');
```

_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Handle implicit politeness for `<output>` elements in level filtering.**

Line 36 includes `<output>` as a candidate, but Lines 47-55 never infer its effective level. `expect(...).toHaveLiveRegion({ level: 'polite' })` can incorrectly fail for `<output>` regions.



<details>
<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-    const role = el.getAttribute('role');
+    const role = el.getAttribute('role');
+    const isOutput = el.tagName.toLowerCase() === 'output';

     let effectiveLevel: string | null = ariaLive;
     if (!effectiveLevel) {
-      if (role === 'status' || role === 'log') {
+      if (role === 'status' || role === 'log' || isOutput) {
         effectiveLevel = 'polite';
       }
       if (role === 'alert') {
         effectiveLevel = 'assertive';
       }
     }
```
</details>

