In `@code/core/src/shared/utils/toHaveLiveRegion.ts` around lines 47 - 55, The
level-inference block for computing effectiveLevel doesn't treat <output> as
implicitly polite, so toHaveLiveRegion can falsely fail for output elements;
update the logic that sets effectiveLevel (the branch using role === 'status' ||
role === 'log' and role === 'alert') to include role === 'output' in the polite
case (i.e., treat 'status', 'log', and 'output' as polite) while keeping 'alert'
-> 'assertive' behavior, referencing the effectiveLevel, ariaLive and role
identifiers to locate the change.
```

